# TRADER — environment contract. Copy to .env and fill in; .env is gitignored and stays so.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ and EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefixes are inlined into client bundles: public, literally.
#
# Three environments, three homes; a value never moves between them through a file.
#   Local       this .env: the compose database and Clerk's development keys. Nothing else
#               loads it but the repository's own entry points; no vendor CLI reads it.
#   Staging     Vercel's Preview variables (the deployment) and the owner's macOS Keychain
#               (commands run from this machine, through wrappers; RULES, Toolbox). Never
#               written here: tests and the seed refuse to run while DATABASE_URL is set.
#   Production  Vercel's Production variables and the owner's password manager. The owner's.
# The phone app's EXPO_PUBLIC_ values will be EAS environment variables, not this file.

# Local Postgres, read by docker-compose.yml through `pnpm db:up`.
# Pick any password; it never leaves this machine.
POSTGRES_USER=trader
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
POSTGRES_DB=trader

# Database connection, read by packages/db/src/env.ts (the Drizzle client, drizzle-kit, tests,
# the seed).
# Unset or empty: the three POSTGRES_* variables above reach the compose container on
# 127.0.0.1:5432. Set: used verbatim and the POSTGRES_* variables are not required (Neon).
# Tests and the seed refuse to run while DATABASE_URL is set: they commit fixtures and create
# databases, and belong on the compose server only.
# A deployment's value is the pooled endpoint with trader_app as the login. Migrations and
# onboarding take the direct endpoint as the owner, typed into the owner's shell for that one
# command and never stored here (packages/db/README.md).
DATABASE_URL=
# Driver behind the Drizzle client; `pg` is the only value, deployed as well.
DATABASE_DRIVER=pg
# Connections one server instance may hold; blank is 10. Sized against the database's limit.
DATABASE_POOL_MAX=

# Clerk, the identity provider, read by apps/web/src/server/clerk-env.ts and by Clerk's own
# code. Both keys are needed; with either missing or malformed this server has no Clerk, every
# protected call answers 401 and roster.invite invites no one. The publishable key is public,
# the secret key is not. A development instance's keys start pk_test_ / sk_test_.
# The Clerk instance itself must add four claims to its session token (Dashboard, Sessions,
# Customize session token), which apps/web/src/server/clerk-identity.ts reads:
#   {"email":"{{user.primary_email_address}}","email_verified":"{{user.email_verified}}",
#    "phone_number":"{{user.primary_phone_number}}","phone_number_verified":"{{user.phone_number_verified}}"}
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
# The origins a session may have been issued to, comma-separated, each a bare origin
# (scheme, host, port; no path). Blank leaves the check to Clerk's default.
CLERK_AUTHORIZED_PARTIES=

# Sentry, the error reporter behind ErrorReporter, read by apps/web/src/server/deploy-env.ts.
# The project's DSN: https, a key, a host and a numeric project. Public by Sentry's own
# definition (it can only submit events). Blank: reports go to stderr alone, as on a
# development machine. Only the minimized event is ever sent (apps/web, sentry-event.ts).
SENTRY_DSN=

# Development identity, read by packages/api/src/core/dev-identity.ts and apps/web/src/server/identity.ts.
# It takes Clerk's place: where it is on, nothing of Clerk runs, /sign-in answers 404 and an
# invitation tells no provider. Under NODE_ENV=production it is never consulted, whatever is set.
# Blank is off. `enabled` trusts the x-trader-dev-subject header with x-trader-dev-email,
# x-trader-dev-phone (a +1 E.164 number) or both, or the
# trader-dev-email cookie set by POST /dev-signin (subject `dev:` + the email lowercased), as a
# verified login, and only under NODE_ENV=development or test; under any other NODE_ENV the API
# refuses the request and /dev-signin answers 404.
TRADER_DEV_IDENTITY=

# Kill switch, read by packages/api/src/core/status.ts. Server-only, never EXPO_PUBLIC_. Blank is
# normal; `read_only` holds pushes, `paused` holds all sync. Builds below a minimum (a positive
# integer; blank is 1) are told to update. An invalid value answers `paused` and is reported.
# Deployed values change only with a new deployment.
TRADER_SYNC_MODE=
TRADER_MIN_BUILD_IOS=
TRADER_MIN_BUILD_ANDROID=

# A deployment (NODE_ENV=production) refuses to start unless DATABASE_URL, both Clerk keys,
# CLERK_AUTHORIZED_PARTIES and SENTRY_DSN are set and well formed, TRADER_DEV_IDENTITY is
# blank and the three kill-switch variables parse (apps/web/src/server/deploy-env.ts).
# VERCEL_ENV and VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA are the platform's own, never set by hand: they name
# the environment and the release on a report.
